UPDATE companies SET description='Green Gables Furniture operates from Bradford, Illinois. The company traces its roots to the 1980s when a family-owned operation began building furniture out of a three-car garage. It remains proudly family owned today, with no outside ownership changes mentioned.

The firm manufactures solid wood furniture in the United States, working with reclaimed barnwood, live-edge hardwoods, and species such as Walnut, Cherry, Hickory, and White Oak. Production combines traditional woodworking techniques with contemporary design, incorporating steel accents and preserving natural character marks like knots, saw marks, and grain variation. The company notes that these features are not imperfections but what make each piece one of a kind. Specific facility size, headcount, and annual volume are not disclosed.

End customers purchase pieces for home use, ranging from rustic Western styles to clean, modern collections such as the Silverton and Steelbound lines.

The company emphasizes distinctive design, authentic materials, and craftsmanship that can be seen and felt. Its stated goal is to build beautiful, honest furniture with real character — pieces that don’t simply fill a room but become part of it — and to build them well enough to be enjoyed for generations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solid wood furniture manufacturing", "Reclaimed barnwood milling", "Live-edge slab processing", "Steel and wood fabrication", "Hand finishing and detailing"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Home furnishings"], "materials": ["Reclaimed barnwood", "Walnut", "Cherry", "Hickory", "White Oak", "Live-edge hardwoods", "Steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned since the 1980s", "Solid wood furniture made in the USA", "Reclaimed barnwood and live-edge hardwoods", "Combines time-honored woodworking with fresh ideas", "Sold through a long-standing dealer network"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Bradford, Illinois -> db", "Founded in 1980s, family-owned, started in three-car garage -> /about-us", "Remains proudly family owned -> /about-us", "Manufactures solid wood furniture in USA -> /about-us", "Materials: reclaimed barnwood, Walnut, Cherry, Hickory, White Oak, live-edge hardwoods, steel -> /about-us", "Combines traditional woodworking with contemporary design, steel accents -> /about-us", "Sells through dealer network -> /about-us", "Goal: build beautiful, honest furniture with character for generations -> /about-us", "Collections: Silverton, Steelbound, etc. -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Green Gables creates solid wood furniture in the USA", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='green-gables-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Green Leaf Solar operates from Columbia, Missouri. The company is owned by Ryan Roe, who has a passion for renewable energy and a mathematics background for designing optimal systems. The founding year is not publicly disclosed.

Green Leaf Solar designs and installs photovoltaic systems for homes and businesses, and assists customers in securing incentives, rebates, and financing to minimize upfront cost. The company offers a 10-year "Done Right" guarantee on installations, a 5-year labor warranty on part failure, and notes that solar components carry 10- to 30-year manufacturer warranties. The installation team includes a chief troubleshooter and two solar technicians alongside the owner and sales manager.

The company serves residential and commercial customers in the Columbia, Missouri area, helping homeowners and businesses reduce electricity costs and hedge against rising energy rates.

Green Leaf Solar emphasizes risk reduction for customers by handling incentive paperwork and offering long-term warranties. Owner Ryan Roe applies a mathematics background to system design for cost effectiveness, while Sales Manager Jay Hasheider brings over three decades of utility experience from Columbia Water and Light, including state recognition for resource stewardship.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design", "Solar installation", "Incentive, rebate, and loan identification", "System financing assistance", "Post-installation warranty service"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Renewable energy installation"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Finds all available incentives, rebates, and loans to minimize payback time", "10-year ''Done Right'' installation guarantee", "5-year labor warranty on part failure", "Owner''s mathematics background for optimal system design", "Sales manager with 30+ years utility experience"], "facts_used": ["Location: Columbia, Missouri -> db", "Owner: Ryan Roe -> /about", "Sales Manager: Jay Hasheider with 30+ years at Columbia Water and Light -> /about", "Team members: Martin Podolak, Alex, Carlos -> /about", "Specializes in incentives, rebates, loans -> /", "10-year ''Done Right'' guarantee, 5-year labor warranty, 10-30 year parts warranty -> /", "Serves homes and businesses in Columbia area -> /", "Ryan Roe mathematics background for system design -> /about", "Jay Hasheider Resource Steward Award, utility experience -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Green Leaf Solar specializes in finding all incentives, rebates and loans available. ... We give a 10 year ''Done Right'' Guaranty on all Installs.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='green-leaf-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Green Mountain Semiconductor, Inc. was founded in 2015 in Burlington, Vermont, by three friends and colleagues who began collaborating on semiconductor design projects. The company remains headquartered in Burlington, where its engineering team performs all design work in-house.

The firm provides custom analog, digital, and mixed-signal ASIC design services, with deep expertise in memory design (DRAM, SRAM, emerging non-volatile memory) and compute-in-memory architectures. Its service offerings include AI circuit design, emerging memory development, special-purpose applications, and high-speed interface solutions such as LPDDR4/4X/5 and SPI/QPI PHYs. The team has experience in advanced process nodes, including 7 nm TSMC, and holds seven patents in commodity memory architecture, error correction, and in-memory high-parallel data processing.

Green Mountain Semiconductor serves aerospace and defense, high-performance computing, and medical device markets. In aerospace and defense, it develops radiation-hardened neuromorphic processors for NASA and works on SWaP-optimized sensor-processing chips. For medical devices, it creates low-power integrated circuits for patient monitoring and diagnosis, including neuromorphic edge-computing IP. The company also supports high-performance computing platforms with custom memory and interface IP.

The company emphasizes its 100% U.S.-based design team, with all work performed by employees at its Burlington offices. Its differentiation rests on a combination of memory-design heritage, patented in-memory computing techniques, and a focus on size, weight, and power (SWaP) optimization for demanding applications.', certifications=ARRAY['CMMC 2.0']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom ASIC design (analog, digital, mixed-signal)", "AI circuit design / in-memory computing", "Analog & mixed-signal design (charge pumps, level shifters, H-bridge drivers, low-noise amplifiers)", "Emerging memory development (DRAM, SRAM, NVM)", "Special-purpose application IC development", "High-speed PHY interface design (LPDDR4/4X/5, SPI/QPI)", "Full custom ASIC development (from technology development to test chips)", "Circuit development and product focus", "Neuromorphic processor design (rad-hard)", "Low-power / SWaP-optimized design", "IP development and integration", "Test chip development and yield assessment", "Digital tool flows", "Radiation-tolerant design techniques"], "industries": ["Aerospace and Defense", "High-Performance Computing", "Medical Devices"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% U.S.-based design team (all designs by employees in Burlington, VT)", "Deep memory-design heritage (DRAM, SRAM, emerging NVM) and compute-in-memory expertise", "Seven patents in commodity memory architecture, error correction, and in-memory parallel processing", "Experience with advanced process nodes (7 nm TSMC)", "Radiation-hardened neuromorphic processor development for NASA"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2015 -> db", "Headquarters Burlington, Vermont -> db", "CMMC 2.0 certification achieved -> page ''/''", "Founded by three friends and colleagues -> page ''/''", "Services: Custom ASIC Design, AI Circuit Design, Analog & Mixed Signal Design, Emerging Memory Development, Special Purpose Applications, Interface Solutions -> page ''/''", "Industries served: Aerospace and Defense, High-Performance Computing, Medical Devices -> page ''/''", "100% US-based, all designs performed by own employees at offices in Burlington, VT -> page ''/''", "Seven patents on compute-in-memory architectures -> page ''/''", "Development contracts with NSF and NASA for rad-hard neuromorphic processors -> page ''/''", "Experience with 7nm TSMC process node -> page ''/''", "Focus on SWaP-optimized solutions -> page ''/''"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a design services firm specializing in cutting-edge semiconductor solutions.", "founded_year": "2015", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='green-mountain-semiconductor-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Green Mountain Solar was founded in 2017 in South Burlington, Vermont, with a commitment to customers and a more sustainable future. The company operates from its headquarters in South Burlington and a second office in East Dorset, serving the entire state.

The firm provides full-service solar design, project management, and installation for residential and commercial customers. Its offerings include rooftop and ground-mounted solar arrays, battery backup systems, heat pump installations, and electric vehicle charger setups. An in-house service team handles post-installation maintenance and support.

Green Mountain Solar works primarily with Vermont homeowners and businesses seeking renewable energy solutions. Projects referenced in customer testimonials range from a 13.7 kWh ground-mounted array in Woodstock to association rooftop installations and Tesla storage system retrofits. The company also partners with financing providers to offer loan options.

