UPDATE companies SET description='HMB Electronics, a women-owned small business, is headquartered in North Haven, Connecticut, where it services the Northeast region of the United States. The company was established to meet growing demand for expedited shipments and regional service by leveraging a vast network of electronic component suppliers both domestically and internationally.

As a stocking distributor, HMB Electronics carries name-brand electronic components — including integrated circuits, resistors, transistors, capacitors, connectors, and computer peripherals — from manufacturers such as Analog Devices, Texas Instruments, Intel, Xilinx, and Maxim. It offers same-day shipping on stocked items and next-day expedited delivery. For hard-to-find or end-of-life parts, the company sources through domestic and international channels, purchases excess inventory from reputable suppliers, and provides cross-referencing support. Component authenticity is verified via a partner testing facility on the East Coast, and manufacturer traceability certificates are supplied when available. Inventory is held in a climate-controlled, anti-static warehouse with continuous monitoring.

The distributor serves government agencies, original equipment manufacturers (OEMs), contract manufacturers (CMs), and both franchised and non-franchised distributors. Its customer base spans the military, information technology, and OEM sectors, with the company noting it works with industry leaders in those fields.

HMB Electronics emphasizes rapid fulfillment, traceability, and quality assurance as key differentiators. It maintains AS5553 compliance for counterfeit electronic parts avoidance, detection, mitigation, and disposition, and aims to guarantee authentic components with manufacturer traceability wherever possible.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','AS5553']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electronic component distribution", "Obsolete/EOL component sourcing", "Excess inventory purchasing", "Cross-referencing", "Component testing (via partner facility)", "Traceability documentation", "Same-day shipping", "Expedited shipping", "AS5553 counterfeit avoidance compliance"], "industries": ["Government", "OEM", "Contract Manufacturer", "Franchised Distributors", "Non-franchised Distributors", "Military", "Information Technology"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping for stocked items; next-day expedited shipping; obsolete parts sourced in a matter of days", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day shipping on stocked parts", "Next-day expedited shipping available", "Domestic and international sourcing for obsolete and end-of-life components", "Third-party component testing for authenticity verification", "Manufacturer traceability certificates provided"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in North Haven, CT -> /about", "Women-Owned Small Business -> /about", "Stocking distributor of name brand electronic components -> /", "Same-day shipping on stocked parts -> /", "Next-day expedited shipping -> /", "Sourcing obsolete and EOL components domestically and internationally -> /about", "Excess inventory purchasing -> /services", "Cross-referencing services -> /services", "Component testing via East Coast testing facility -> /about", "Manufacturer traceability certificates -> /about", "Climate-controlled, anti-static warehouse with full-time monitoring -> /about", "Serves government, OEM, CM, franchised and non-franchised distributors -> /", "Industries served: Military, IT, OEM -> /", "ISO 9001 certification -> db", "AS5553 compliance certificate -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "HMB Electronics is a stocking distributor of name brand electronic components with discount pricing and same day shipments.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/hmb-electronics/"], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='hmb-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Haake Manufacturing Co. operates from a 100,000-square-foot facility in De Soto, Missouri. The company was founded in 1948 by Fred C. Haake Sr., a German-trained machinist, and his wife Elfriede, who opened a small tool-and-die shop in their St. Louis garage with a single punch press. In 1963, the second generation — Fred Jr. and Lorraine Haake — relocated the business to De Soto and added a dedicated trucking operation to control delivery. Today the company is led by fourth-generation family member Jay Rieker, maintaining continuous family ownership since inception.

The shop provides full-service precision sheet metal fabrication under one roof. Core processes include CNC laser cutting (up to 10,000 watts), CNC punching with 360-degree tool rotation, combined punch/laser cells that form and contour in a single setup, CNC press brake forming with six-axis back gauges, metal stamping on AIDA cells up to 160 tons (supplemented by 5–150-ton presses), robotic MIG/MAG welding of steel, stainless steel, and aluminum, and a fully automated powder coating line with six-stage wash, infrared pre-processing, and zirconium pretreatment. Secondary services cover assembly, hardware insertion, and finish coordination.

Haake serves manufacturers across the United States, with historical roots in the St. Louis industrial base. The company now supports reshoring programs and just-in-time inventory strategies for OEMs and contract assemblers requiring domestic supply-chain stability.

The founding principle — deliver parts that arrive on time and fit flawlessly — remains the stated differentiator. Haake emphasizes its central U.S. location, in-house freight, and solar-assisted low operating costs as structural advantages that enable 2-day shipping to either coast, 99% on-time delivery, and defect rates of 292 PPM for fabrication and 0 PPM for powder coating (2025 data).', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC laser cutting", "CNC punching", "CNC punch/laser combination", "CNC press brake forming", "Metal stamping (progressive and single-station)", "Robotic MIG/MAG welding", "Automated powder coating", "Assembly and hardware insertion", "Metal finishing coordination"], "industries": ["Aerospace / defense", "Industrial machinery", "OEM manufacturing", "Contract assembly"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Trumpf CNC systems", "Fiber lasers (up to 10,000 W)", "AIDA punching cells (up to 160 tons)", "Press brakes with automated six-axis back gauges", "Electric press brakes", "Robotic welding cells", "Automated powder coating line (six-stage wash, infrared pre-processing, zirconium pretreatment)"], "volume": "Short to high-volume production runs", "lead_time": "2-day shipping to either coast; faster lead times via central location and in-house freight", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All fabrication, finishing, and assembly processes in a single 100,000 sq ft facility", "Central U.S. location (De Soto, MO) with company-owned freight for 2-day coast-to-coast shipping", "Combined punch/laser machines that form and cut in one workflow \u2014 rare in the St. Louis region", "ISO 9001:2015 certified with published defect rates (292 PPM fabrication, 0 PPM powder coat, 2025)", "Fourth-generation family ownership providing continuity and domestic supply-chain stability"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1948 by Fred C. Haake Sr. and Elfriede in St. Louis garage -> /about", "Relocated to De 