UPDATE companies SET description='Hampshire Controls Corporation was established in 1976 in Dover, New Hampshire. The company designs and manufactures monitoring, data logging, and alarm notification systems for demanding applications, emphasizing "Made in the USA" reliability.

The product line includes NIST-traceable temperature monitors and alarms (configurable with 2 to 8 channels), cryogenic temperature monitors, multi-probe condition monitors, the T° Sentry ALERT data logging and alarm system, Wi-Fi temperature transmitters, biomedical freezer backup systems (liquid CO2 and liquid nitrogen), LN2 level monitors, laboratory air flow monitors, and remote alarm delay modules. Manufacturing services encompass PCB soldering, cable manufacturing, subsystem interfacing, final electronic assembly, electronic testing, burn-in, and NIST-traceable calibration, all performed at the Dover facility. The firm also provides custom mechanical and electrical engineering, firmware development, and communication protocol implementation (BACnet, Modbus, MQTT, HTTP/HTTPS, etc.).

Hampshire Controls serves blood banks, cryogenic biologic storage facilities, vaccine and genetic research laboratories, biopharma production plants, governmental agencies, hospitals, commercial food processing and storage operations, and industrial manufacturers. It also supplies original equipment manufacturers (OEMs) with high-volume temperature monitoring and alarm systems for clinical, food and beverage, water distribution, plumbing, and industrial markets.

The company differentiates itself through in-house design, manufacturing, and calibration capabilities, allowing it to offer both standard and custom-engineered products with NIST-traceable calibration. Its systems are UL LISTED and built to meet NEMA/IP ratings for harsh environments.', certifications=ARRAY['UL LISTED']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Engineering & Manufacturing Services", "Customization of Standard Monitoring/Alarm Systems", "Mechanical and Electrical Engineering", "Firmware Development", "PCB Design (Analog, Digital, Mixed-signal)", "PCB Soldering", "Cable Manufacturing", "Subsystem Interfacing", "Final Electronic Product Assembly", "Electronic Testing", "Burn-in Testing", "NIST-traceable Calibration", "NEMA/IP-rated Enclosure Design", "Private Labeling", "Custom Panel Design", "Microcontroller Selection", "Sensor Data Acquisition, Amplification, Filtering", "Power Supply Design (Line-powered, Battery-powered, Mixed)", "Communication Protocol Implementation (BACnet, Modbus, MQTT, HTTP/HTTPS)", "Wired/Wireless Connectivity (RF, Wi-Fi, Cellular LTE, Ethernet, RS-232/422/485)"], "industries": ["Blood Banks", "Cryogenic Biologic Storage", "Vaccine and Genetic Research Laboratories", "Biopharma Production Facilities", "Governmental Agencies", "Hospitals", "Commercial Food Processing and Storage", "Industrial Manufacturing", "Original Equipment Manufacturers (OEMs)", "Laboratory Research", "Clinical", "Food and Beverage", "Water Distribution and Plumbing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["NIST-traceable calibration on all sensors", "Designed and manufactured in Dover, NH facility", "Custom engineering from concept through production", "UL LISTED products", "Supports industry-standard and proprietary communication protocols"], "facts_used": ["Established in 1976, based in Dover, NH -> /about-us", "Designer and manufacturer of monitoring, logging, alarm systems -> /about-us", "N