UPDATE companies SET description='House of Sharp operates from a 4,000-square-foot shop in Mulvane, Kansas, just south of Wichita. The company was founded in January 2018 by co-owners Ernest Sharp and Rose Hansen after Sharp built a CNC plasma table in the basement of a rental house and Hansen left her 9-to-5 job to pursue creative work.

The shop provides turnkey custom metal fabrication with an in-house team that includes a graphic designer, artist, CAD designer, mechanical engineer, and skilled fabricators. The facility includes a showroom and retail storefront.

Customers range from Kansas businesses to private individuals. Projects have included driveway arches for cemeteries, fireplace wraps for restaurants, patio railings for dining establishments, custom mailbox posts, and mixed-media pieces such as a steel-and-wood stool. The company also sells through an Etsy storefront.

