UPDATE companies SET description='Howard Foods Inc. is headquartered in Danvers, Massachusetts. The company traces its origins to the early 1890s when John F. Howard and his wife Margaret began producing relishes in the kitchen of their Bradford hotel. The business was incorporated in 1924 after Howard sold it to Arthur D. Dickson, and merged with the C.E. Chapin Company in 1926. Since 1990, the company has been under its current ownership, with the sales office relocated to Danvers.

Howard Foods manufactures a line of gourmet condiments that includes Sweet Pepper Relish, Hot Pepper Relish, Green Tomato Piccalilli, Ham Glaze, Garlic Seasoning Juice, and Onion Seasoning Juice. The products are made using traditional recipes that the company says have not changed since the 19th century. The firm also offers pure maple syrup. No details on facility size, headcount, or annual volume are disclosed.

The company serves retail grocery stores throughout New England, foodservice operators such as restaurants, and direct-to-consumer customers through its online store. Its relishes have been used by generations of families and restaurants, and the Sweet Pepper Relish is described as the bestselling sweet pepper relish in the United States.

Howard Foods emphasizes natural ingredients, simplicity, and recipes that have withstood the test of time. Its products earned a Grand Prix at the 1900 International Exhibition in Paris for purity and quality, and the company promotes its relishes as delivering great flavor at value prices without sacrificing quality.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sweet pepper relish manufacturing", "Hot pepper relish manufacturing", "Green tomato piccalilli manufacturing", "Ham glaze manufacturing", "Garlic seasoning juice manufacturing", "Onion seasoning juice manufacturing"], "industries": ["Retail grocery", "Foodservice", "E-commerce"], "materials": ["Red bell peppers", "Green peppers", "Green tomatoes", "Onions", "Brown sugar", "Cider vinegar", "Spices", "Maple syrup"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Recipes unchanged since the 1890s", "Grand Prix award at 1900 Paris International Exhibition for purity and quality", "#1 bestselling sweet pepper relish in America", "Natural ingredients and simplicity as core differentiators", "Sold through New England grocery stores and direct online"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Danvers, Massachusetts -> db", "Founded in early 1890s by John F. Howard and wife Margaret -> /about-us", "Incorporated in 1924 after sale to Arthur D. Dickson -> /about-us", "Merged with C.E. Chapin Company in 1926 -> /about-us", "Current owners since 1990, sales office moved to Danvers -> /about-us", "Products: Sweet Pepper Relish, Hot Pepper Relish, Green Tomato Piccalilli, Ham Glaze, Garlic Seasoning Juice, Onion Seasoning Juice -> /about-us, /", "Recipes unchanged since 19th century -> /about-us", "Grand Prix award in 1900 Paris International Exhibition -> /about-us", "#1 bestselling sweet pepper relish in America -> /", "Natural ingredients, simplicity, recipe withstood test of time -> /", "Serves retail grocery stores in New England, restaurants, online direct -> /", "Maple syrup offered -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "The combined corporations were reorganized in the new Howard Foods plant by the river in Haverhill, under the name of Howard Foods.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='howard-foods-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Huetter Mill & Cabinet operates from Murray, Utah, where it was founded in 1948 by Alfred Huetter, a German immigrant who began building window sash and custom millwork in a chicken coop behind his family home in the 1930s. The business remains family-owned, now led by President Gordon Huetter, Alfred’s son.

The company manufactures custom millwork, stair parts, handrails, and hardwood moldings from a dedicated production facility and showroom in Murray. It stocks moldings in alder, knotty alder, maple, poplar, cherry, and oak, maintains a library of custom knives for unique profiles, and produces curved stairways and complete stair systems. Inventory exceeds $1.2 million, and the firm uses advanced machinery staffed by skilled craftsmen to serve both commercial and high-end residential projects, shipping nationally.

Huetter Mill serves commercial construction, residential new builds, and remodeling markets, with a specialty in historic restoration. Past projects include the Utah Governor’s Mansion, Utah State Capitol, The Children’s Center, and O.C. Tanner renovations. Capabilities extend to schools, hospitals, tenant improvements, court buildings, and correctional facilities.

The company’s stated purpose is to provide a financially sound source for wholesale millwork and commercial shop products at reasonable cost, delivered efficiently by trained employees. Its motto, “Quality and Craftsmanship live in our Name,” reflects the multi-generational commitment to that standard.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom millwork", "Stair parts manufacturing", "Handrail manufacturing", "Hardwood molding production", "Custom cabinetry", "Historic restoration millwork", "Custom knife grinding for moldings", "Curved stair fabrication", "Stairway system assembly", "Wholesale millwork supply", "Commercial project millwork", "Tenant improvement millwork", "Stair installation"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Residential construction", "Remodeling", "Historic restoration", "Education (schools)", "Healthcare (hospitals)", "Government (court buildings, jails)", "Tenant improvements", "Architectural millwork", "Cabinetry"], "materials": ["Alder", "Knotty alder", "Maple", "Poplar", "Cherry", "Oak"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1948 by Alfred Huetter -> /about-us", "Family-owned since founding -> /about-us", "Located in Murray, Utah -> /about-us", "Manufactures custom millwork, stair parts, moldings -> /", "Materials: alder, knotty alder, maple, poplar, cherry, oak -> /about-us", "Inventory over $1.2 million -> /about-us", "Historic restoration projects: Governor''s Mansion, Utah State Capitol, The Children''s Center, O.C. Tanner -> /about-us", "Capabilities: historic renovations, schools, hospitals, tenant improvements, court buildings, jails -> /about-us", "Custom knife library for moldings -> /about-us", "Curved custom stairways and stair systems -> /about-us", "Nationwide shipping -> /", "Purpose: financially sound company for wholesale millwork at reasonable cost -> /about-us", "Motto: Quality and Craftsmanship live in our Name -> /abo