UPDATE companies SET description='Hunt & Noyer Furniture was established in 2013 in the Village of Clarkston, Michigan. The small business takes its name from the surnames of founder Kyle’s parents, DesNoyer and Huntoon, honoring a lineage of Midwestern craftsmen. Kyle launched the company to continue a family tradition of woodworking, building pieces that reflect a respect for heritage and a commitment to enduring quality.

The workshop produces a range of furniture including benches, dining tables, consoles, cabinets, and seating, with a focus on modern design executed through traditional handcrafting methods. They accept custom one-off commissions for private residences as well as larger-scale projects for public and corporate clients. Walnut is a signature material, selected and worked by hand for each piece.

The company serves residential customers, commercial and institutional clients, and interior designers through a trade program. Past projects include custom dining tables for homeowners in Michigan and Illinois, a solid walnut crib for a nursery in Jackson, MI, and consoles used as home-office workstations. Interior designers receive a trade discount on the existing collection.

Hunt & Noyer positions its work as heirloom-quality rather than trend-driven, emphasizing that “trends change, but quality is timeless.” The founder’s personal involvement in design and material selection, along with a philosophy rooted in American craftsmanship, is presented as the core differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cabinets", "Seating", "Tables", "Benches", "Upholstered Bench", "Modern Furniture"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Institutional", "Interior Design"], "materials": ["Walnut"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom one-off commissions and large-scale public/corporate projects", "Trade discounts for interior designers on current collection", "Heirloom-quality furniture handcrafted in Michigan", "Walnut as a specialty wood, hand-selected for each project", "Design philosophy driven by modernism and timeless quality"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2013 -> db", "Headquarters Village of Clarkston, Michigan -> db", "Founder Kyle (DesNoyer and Huntoon lineage) -> homepage", "Handcrafted furniture in Michigan -> homepage", "Custom one-off commissions and large-scale projects -> homepage", "Trade discounts for interior designers -> homepage", "Walnut specialty -> homepage testimonial", "Products: benches, tables, consoles, cabinets, seating -> homepage and capabilities list", "Small business -> description"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We take on everything from custom one-off commissions for private homes to large scale public and corporate projects.", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='hunt-noyer-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ICON Injection Molding, Inc. was founded in 2001 in Phoenix, Arizona, by three brothers—Danny, Philip, and Steve Kleitsch. The Kleitsches had worked in their father’s injection molding and tooling shop since the late 1970s, learning tool building and supplier relationships. After their father sold the business, the brothers launched their own family-owned company, naming it ICON after becoming the first custom molder in Arizona to run electric‑hybrid molding machines. Their motto, “Excellence from Art to Part,” was coined early by Danny Kleitsch and still guides the business.

The company provides custom plastic injection molding solutions, including tooling, machining, assembly, and secondary operations. Its facility houses 42 presses ranging from 15 to 720 tons, with capacity for further growth. Capabilities span automation, clean‑room molding, overmolding, rotary (vertical) molding, and custom packaging. A scientific molding approach uses statistical analysis to drive process stability, supported by a quality lab equipped with Keyence 3‑D inspection (to 0.00008 in tolerance), capability studies (CPK), Gage R&R, first‑article inspection, and IQ/OQ/PQ validation. ICON also offers global sourcing through domestic and offshore strategic partnerships, and a campus expansion dubbed “ICON 4” is underway.

ICON serves customers worldwide, from local Phoenix businesses to international clients, delivering both “Made in USA” parts and cost‑effective offshore options.

The founders started ICON to apply a scientific, engineering‑based methodology to molding—preventing problems rather than detecting them. The family‑owned structure, with over 100 combined years of industry experience, underpins a culture of continual improvement and point‑of‑use quality.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Tooling & machining", "Secondary operations", "Automation", "Clean room molding", "Overmolding", "Rotary (vertical) molding", "Custom packaging", "Scientific molding", "Capability studies (CPK)", "Gage R&R", "First article inspection", "X-bar and R charting", "Pareto charting", "IQ/OQ/PQ validation", "Assembly", "Global sourcing (domestic/offshore partnerships)", "Keyence 3-D inspection"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["42 injection molding presses (15\u2013720 tons)", "Electric-hybrid molding machines", "Keyence 3-D inspection system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Keyence 3-D inspection up to 0.00008 in", "built_on": ["Scientific molding with statistical process control", "42 presses from 15 to 720 tons", "Keyence 3\u2011D inspection to 0.00008 in tolerance", "Family\u2011owned with 100+ combined years of experience", "Domestic and offshore strategic partnerships"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2001 by Danny, Philip, Steve Kleitsch -> /about-us", "Family-owned and operated -> /about-us", "Headquarters Phoenix, Arizona -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /about-us", "42 presses 15-720 tons -> /services", "Scientific molding approach with statistical analysis -> /services", "Keyence 3-D inspection up to 0.00008 tolerance -> /services", "Electric-hybrid molding machines first in Arizona -> /about-us", "Global capabilities with domestic/offshore partnerships -> /services", "Over 100 combined years industry experience -> /about-us", "New expansion ICON 4 coming soon -> /", "Motto Excellence from Art to Part -> /about-us", "Quality lab with CPK, Gage R&R, First Article, IQ/OQ/PQ -> /services", "Clean room molding, overmolding, rotary molding, custom packaging -> /services", "Assembly mentioned -> /about-us", "Tooling & machining -> /services", "Secondary operations -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "ICON Injection Molding is a family-owned and operated manufacturing company dedicated to providing products and services that exceed the expectations of our customers.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='icon-injection-molding-inc-shipping-receiving' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='IEG Plastics LLC was founded in 2004 in Bellefontaine, Ohio. The company operates as a supplier of plastic parts and assemblies, serving primarily the automotive and consumer goods sectors.

The company provides plastic injection molding, mold building, and product design services under one roof. Its mold building capacity handles tools up to 20,000 pounds, and it offers both domestic and Asian mold sourcing with U.S.-based engineering changes and repair. Production capabilities include tight-tolerance molding to ±0.02 mm (±0.000787 in), insert molding, overmolding, robotic part handling, sonic welding, and assembly. An environmentally controlled metrology lab houses a Brown & Sharpe CMM, Micro-VU Vertex 311HC, Zeiss 3D light scanner, and other inspection equipment. Design work uses SolidWorks, Catia, and Pro/E, with DFM and Moldflow analysis available. The firm also runs prototypes and low-volume functional parts via 3D printing.

IEG Plastics serves the automotive, consumer goods, and sporting goods industries. Automotive work includes safety components that require adherence to strict quality standards such as APQP and PPAP. Consumer and sporting goods projects leverage the company’s experience with precision, high-volume parts.

The company emphasizes partnerships aimed at increasing productivity and reducing total cost. It cites in-house engineering and design, streamlined processes for short lead times, a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015, and the use of RJG process control and advanced scanning technology as differentiators. Operating on the Traction Entrepreneurial Operating System, IEG Plastics focuses on accountability and continuous improvement to deliver dock-to-stock quality on time.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Mold building (up to 20,000 lbs)", "Engineering / product design", "Design software: SolidWorks, Catia, Pro/E", "DFM analysis", "Moldflow analysis", "Prototyping", "3D printing", "Low-volume functional parts", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "Robotics integration", "Assembly", "Sonic welding", "Statistical process analysis (Minitab, IQMS)", "Gage R&R analysis", "PV testing", "Gage calibration (NIST traceable)", "Metrology: CMM (Brown & Sharpe), Micro-VU Vertex, Zeiss 3D light scanner, profilometer, force gage, environmental test chamber", "RJG process control", "Tight tolerance molding (\u00b10.02 mm)", "APQP / PPAP", "AIAG standards compliance", "Mold repair and engineering changes (USA)"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Consumer goods", "Sporting goods"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Brown & Sharpe CMM", "Micro-VU Vertex 311HC", "Zeiss 3D Light Scanner", "Tenney Environmental test chamber", "Force Gage", "Profilometer", "RJG Process Control sensors", "Blue Light Scanner", "Checking fixtures"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.02 mm (\u00b10.000787 in)", "built_on": ["In-house engineering, tooling, molding, and assembly under one roof", "Tight-tolerance molding to \u00b10.02 mm with RJG process control", "Environmentally controlled metrology lab with CMM, optical scanner, and 3D light scanner", "ISO 9001:2015 certified QMS with full APQP/PPAP and AIAG compliance", "U.S.-based mold support shop for engineering changes and repairs"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2004 -> db", "Headquartered in Bellefontaine, Ohio -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "Plastic injection molding -> /capabilities", "Mold building up to 20,000 lbs -> /capabilities", "Tight tolerance molding \u00b10.02 mm -> /capabilities", "Industries: automotive, consumer goods, sporting goods -> /capabilities", "Equipment: Brown & Sharpe CMM, Micro-VU Vertex, Zeiss 3D Light Scanner, Tenney Environmental test chamber, Force Gage, Profilometer -> /quality", "RJG Process Control -> /capabilities", "In-house metrology lab -> /quality", "Turnkey solutions from design to assembly -> /about-us", "Operates on Traction EOS -> /about-us", "USA and Asian mold building -> /capabilities", "Insert molding, over molding, robotics, sonic welding -> /capabilities", "Design software: SolidWorks, Catia, Pro E -> /capabilities", "DFM, Moldflow analysis -> /capabilities", "Prototyping, 3D printing, low volume functional parts -> /capabilities", "Statistical analysis with Minitab and IQMS -> /capabilities", "GR&R analysis, PV testing, Gage calibration -> /capabilities", "APQP, PPAP, AIAG standards -> /capabilities", "Calibration traceable to NIST -> /capabilities", "Value-added assembly -> /about-us", "Commitment to on-time delivery of defect-free product -> /quality", "Community involvement -> /about-us", "No ownership tags stated -> db", "No employee count stated -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a proud supplier of plastic parts and assemblies to the automotive and consumer goods industries.", "founded_year": "2004", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ieg-plastics-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1963, Industrial Electronic Supply (IES) has been headquartered in Baton Rouge, Louisiana for over six decades.

IES operates as a distributor of industrial electronic components across five core categories: industrial controls, automation, drives, power distribution, and instrumentation. Its catalog features products from Siemens, Emerson, Turck, Banner Engineering, Rittal, Weidmüller, and Flowline, among others. Beyond product supply, IES provides technical services such as IO-Link integration support, condition monitoring for electrical control cabinets, predictive maintenance consulting, and 24/7 cloud-based monitoring.

Concrete examples from its product announcements include cooling units for airport baggage-handling systems and port cranes, automation packages for a Texas brewery, pump control panels for irrigation and oilfield applications, and vibration sensors for predictive maintenance on production machinery.

